    <dt>
      <strong>Updates</strong>
    </dt>
    <dd>I will normally update my book spreadsheet about once a week, and those changes will get pushed here.
    </dd>

    <dt>
      <strong>Ratings</strong>
    </dt>
    <dd>Generally a 5 is an average book in my scoring system. Anything under a 5 is probably not worth reading in my opinion. Obviously lots of factors go into a score, such as external life events,
      as well as narrator if it is an audiobook. A lot of stuff ends up around 7 since that is an "Averagely good" book. An important note is that I give books a score right after I finish reading them,
      and sometimes my feelings on a book change over time. That is why you will see in my book lists that my favorite books are not always ordered exactly by the score I give them. The longer I have done this, I have slowly become a slightly harsher
      grader, so books that I gave a good score a few years ago would most likely receive a lower score if I read it today.
    </dd>

    <dt>
      <strong>Summaries</strong>
    </dt>
    <dd>I started writing book summaries in the middle of 2025. The more I enjoy the book generally the more effort I will put into the summary.
      I am still trying to find a balance of how much detail to include. Some, like Ship of Magic, are very detailed but that makes them super long and take a lot of time to write.
    </dd>

    <dt>
      <strong>Trivia</strong>
    </dt>
    <dd>
      I love trivia but did not start writing down trivia questions about books until May of 2026. From now on I will try to get at least a couple for most books that I read.
    </dd>

    <dt>
      <strong>Time</strong>
    </dt>
    <dd>
      I started tracking what books I read in a document the summer of 2022, then in 2024 expanded to a spreadsheet so I could keep track of more information about each book. Anything from before 2022 is just based on my recall. Obviously there are more books I read before I started keeping track of them, but I only added the ones I remembered and felt confident giving a score. I have been trying to reread a lot of series that I read 
      when I was younger and see how they hold up.
      
      I first started tracking the days it took me to read books with Shadows of Self in September of 2022, so everything before that is mostly just a generic number of days filled in to normalize the data. I put them at about the right dates and just set everything for 
      for 5 or 6 days, since that tends to be my average reading time for normal length books.
    </dd>

